From: LuoRain <luotianyi@luotianyi.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:16:21 +0800
Subject: chore(wayland): allow setting input region in SSD

Upstream drops the window shape's input region on the root surface of a
toplevel that uses server-side decorations, where the compositor owns the
shape. The same early return also dropped regions an embedder sets through
PlatformWindow::SetInputRegion(), so Electron's setInputRegion() and
setIgnoreMouseEvents() had no effect, and their resets could not restore
input.

Guard only the shape path instead, so explicit regions and resets are
applied while the compositor keeps ownership of the decoration area.

Kept downstream rather than sent upstream: the early return exists so that
Chromium's own frame-derived region is not applied under server-side
decorations, where the compositor owns the frame; deleting it would clip
input against a shape the client does not own. Guarding the shape path keeps
that behaviour and only lets explicit regions through, which Chromium itself
never sets on such a toplevel. The change is behaviour-preserving for
Chromium, so it could be proposed as a contract fix for embedders, but with
no in-tree caller its only motivation is Electron's setInputRegion(), and it
stays a patch until upstream has a reason of its own.

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_toplevel_window.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_toplevel_window.cc
index ddd0ea13df37a4db1d024bb0c1fe0aebe26354ef..e669f2e9199fa001bb3c7593c744a82246eacc08 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_toplevel_window.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_toplevel_window.cc
@@ -1054,8 +1054,14 @@ void WaylandToplevelWindow::UpdateWindowMask() {
           ? opaque_region_px_
           : (IsOpaqueWindow() ? std::optional<std::vector<gfx::Rect>>(region)
                               : std::nullopt));
-  root_surface()->set_input_region(input_region_px_ ? input_region_px_
-                                                    : region);
+  // With server-side decorations the compositor draws the frame, so it also
+  // owns the window shape; clipping input against one here would fight it.
+  // The explicit regions set through SetInputRegion() are applied directly and
+  // are not affected.
+  if (!ShouldUseNativeFrame()) {
+    root_surface()->set_input_region(input_region_px_ ? input_region_px_
+                                                      : region);
+  }
 }
 
 void WaylandToplevelWindow::UpdateSessionStateIfNeeded() {
